                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a93a85b-8ef2-3882-a64a-4ac757773e34",
                        "entry_id": "0dd8c002-5da7-3189-ab0f-78c2abc404e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A key that can open several locks, but fewer than a master key."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "attributive",
                            "sometimes"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7c5b149-62fb-4c2d-b3ca-b34821fda472",
                                "sense_id": "7a93a85b-8ef2-3882-a64a-4ac757773e34",
                                "text": "In an office, a submaster might open all doors in the accounting department; in an industrial facility, it might open all locks in the loading dock area."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f83fa5a4-ed02-49ca-b677-e019e7231481",
                                "sense_id": "7a93a85b-8ef2-3882-a64a-4ac757773e34",
                                "text": "Do not point specifically at the executives but find out what the cost estimates are for rekeying a submaster space or the entire facility when one of these keys gets lost […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d8edc62-6acb-4599-b462-e3be3045eecb",
                                "sense_id": "7a93a85b-8ef2-3882-a64a-4ac757773e34",
                                "text": "The use of masters and submasters will enable suites of rooms to be controlled by one key."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f01793c5-b8e6-3b52-afdf-702c40b533cc",
                        "entry_id": "0dd8c002-5da7-3189-ab0f-78c2abc404e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A copy of a master copy of a recording, generally kept for archival purposes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4dc1ec76-8c1d-4336-8208-a0755e1dcb76",
                                "sense_id": "f01793c5-b8e6-3b52-afdf-702c40b533cc",
                                "text": "Unlike cue or group information, submasters usually actively exist and don't need to be created. Methods for recording channel information into different submasters may vary between consoles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7999d677-9344-4dfa-b93d-3e5262abd20a",
                                "sense_id": "f01793c5-b8e6-3b52-afdf-702c40b533cc",
                                "text": "In Edward's absence, Sonny Boy learned to press the discs at Chariot Records. He mastered a process of producing gold-molded submasters that could be played on the phonographs people were now buying for their homes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b32951e-ed2c-3194-971d-df21d4ca8704",
                        "entry_id": "0dd8c002-5da7-3189-ab0f-78c2abc404e1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A secondary or subsidiary schoolmaster."
                        ],
